/*!

*\page function Function Definition
*
*Generic Function Implementation and declaration.
* Functions allow the user to structure their programs in segments of codes to perform individual tasks. 
* They don't share the same global variables. If any script program wants to send a value or variable to the function, user must make them as an argument to the function and function call<BR>
* They do not share the same global variables. If a script program wants to send a value or variable to a function, the user must pass it as an argument in the function call.<BR>
*<br>Functions must be defined in the beginning of the script program. This will allow the system to save the definitions. Later when they are called using "Call" statement, they are executed.
<br> <span style='color:blue'><em><B>Some notes:</B></em></span><br>
* <ul>
* <li>Global variable cannot be accessed inside functions. </li>
* <li>GPIO and other peripherals can be accessed inside functions, they are visible everywhere as they are shared in the system.</li>
* <li>If you want to access (a) global variable(s), send the variable name or the value as an argument to the function.</li>
* <li>Execution of a function might be slower than running the code without a function. Global variables are backed up before calling the function.</li>
* </ul>
*<span style='color:blue'><em><H4> Syntax: </H4></em></span>
*<B> Function function_name(arg1, arg2 ..arg5) { ...code ...}</B><BR>
* - <b>arg1,..arg5:</b> Arguments provided to the function. It could be a string, number, a variable of array, a variable of numbers
*
*<span style='color:blue'><em><B>
*Warning:
*</B> </em> </span>
*
*&nbsp;	Function names cannot be longer than 20 bytes. This limitation restricts the size of the number generated by the hash calculator. Keep this limit in mind when writing a script program.
*
*<span style='color:blue'><em><B>
*Example:
*</B> </em> </span>
*
*function myFirstF(delay_between_pulses){<br>
*&nbsp;	put PA_4,1;<br>
*&nbsp;	delay delay_between_pulses,mSec;<br>
*&nbsp;	put_PA_4,0<br>
*&nbsp;	delay delay_between_pulses,mSec;<br>
}
*<br>
*.....SCRIPT PROGRAM ...<br>
*..<br>
*..<br>
*..<br>
*<br>
*myvariable=10; <br>
*while(1){<br>
*&nbsp;call myFirstF(myvariable);<br>
*}
*<br>
*

*<span style='color:blue'><em><B> 

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<hr />
<p>&nbsp;</p>

*Another example:
*</B> </em> </span>

create_reg myreg PA_10,PB_3,PB_5,PB_4,PB_10,PA_8,PA_9,PC_7<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  <span style='color:green'> rem Function definition.</span><br>
*function myfunc(){  
<span style='color:green'>rem An array variable.</span><br>
 &nbsp;snow[]={0b11111111,0b11111110,0b11111100,0b11111000,0b11110001,0b11100011,0b11000111,0b10001111,0b00011111,0b00111111,0b011111111};<br>
   &nbsp;for(i=0,i<=8,i++){<br>
   &nbsp;&nbsp;  <span style='color:green'> rem Loop.</span><br>
    &nbsp;&nbsp;put myreg, snow[i];<br>
    &nbsp;&nbsp;delay 200,msec<br>
  &nbsp;}<br>
}<br>
<br>
<br>
while(1)  <br>
{<br>
&nbsp;  <span style='color:green'>rem call the function.</span><br>
  &nbsp;call myfunc();<br>
}<br>
* 	 
*/
